Description: khatru: register live listeners before stored queries

Khatru runs a REQ filter's stored query before it registers the live
listener. A client CLOSE arriving during the (possibly slow) stored
query finds nothing to remove, and the listener lingers until
disconnect. Fix: register all listeners before running stored queries;
clean up listeners on filter rejection.

Note: this changes the ordering assumption that some server
implementations may depend on (e.g. gap-buffer mechanisms that
expect the listener to be added after the query). Such implementations
need to be updated to handle the new ordering.

--- a/khatru/handlers.go
+++ b/khatru/handlers.go
@@ -299,20 +299,30 @@
